  "final_message": "The converter is built, but I haven't built the Docker image or started the app, because Docker isn't available here. I did build the frontend with `npm run build`, and I exercised the API with Flask's test client. The test covered:\n- encoding and decoding, including empty text and non-ASCII text;\n- register and login, a duplicate username, and a wrong password;\n- saving a conversion, paging, the 401 on `/api/conversions` without a token, and a user trying to delete another user's entry.\n\nI didn't open the frontend in a browser.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`):\n- **Storage:** SQLite at `data/app.db`.\n- **Tokens:** login issues a random bearer token, stored hashed, and a token can be revoked.\n- **Errors:** every API error is JSON in the form `{\"error\": ...}`.\n- **Beyond the spec:** I added `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` so the frontend can show the signed-in username and sign out properly.\n- **Choices the spec left open:**\n  - Usernames are case-insensitive, so registering `A` after `a` returns 409.\n  - Whitespace inside base64 input is ignored when decoding.\n  - Previews are cut at 100 characters.\n  - `page_size` is capped at 100 and defaults to 20.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src/`):\n- **Layout:** the register and sign-in forms, the username with a sign-out button, two text areas with Encode, Decode and copy buttons, and the API's error message for invalid input.\n- **Signed-in features:** a \"Save to history\" switch, plus a history list with delete buttons and paging.\n- **Styling:** Tailwind v4 utility classes only. I added the Tailwind packages to `frontend/package.json` and refreshed `frontend/package-lock.json`, and the only CSS file is `src/index.css`, which just imports Tailwind.\n\nI also added a `.gitignore`.",
